Overlap analysis
We should measure the actual holdings overlap between each proposed fund and your existing investments.

For example:

A Nifty 500 index fund plus a flexi-cap fund can create substantial large-cap duplication.

A value fund can hold many of the same companies as a broad-market index.

A value fund and a contra fund may express similar underlying investment bets.

A sector fund can increase concentration even when you own several other schemes.

We'll look at overlapping stock weights, sector exposures and common risk factors—not merely count the number of funds.

Official sources such as AMFI provide scheme performance, NAV history, fund disclosures, AUM information and other research data. The latest AMC factsheet and portfolio disclosure will be important evidence in each assessment. 

